Fresh Pi session: REDESIGN THE NEXT CORRECTION AFTER A LOOP FAILURE.

Inputs:
- User prompt and accepted initial design: {{run.dir}}/prompt/ and {{run.dir}}/design/
- Initial design interrogation: {{run.dir}}/design-interrogation/
- Current worktree diff and commit history: {{run.worktree-dir}}
- Round-stamped execution, validation, and review evidence: {{run.dir}}/execution/, {{run.dir}}/validation/, and {{run.dir}}/review/
- Earlier failure-design guidance, when present: {{run.dir}}/failure-design/

The current working directory is the isolated worktree.

Goal:
Diagnose why the loop just failed and give the next implementer a concrete, architecture-aware correction design instead of another unguided retry.

Rules:
- Do not edit source or tests, run artifacts outside the files listed below, commits, or branches.
- Identify only the newest round-stamped issue file across execution, validation, and review as the authoritative current failure. Older evidence may explain history but is not an accumulated backlog.
- Inspect the current diff, relevant source, tests, and prior attempts. Distinguish the root cause from the failing symptom and from incidental noise.
- Reconsider the solution boundary. Search for existing abstractions or parallel implementations and explicitly guard against duplicating code, policy, schemas, state, or control flow.
- Explain why the prior approach failed or stalled and which validated work should be preserved.
- Produce one recommended correction design with exact files or boundaries to inspect/change, tests that should fail then pass, deterministic acceptance criteria, and any approach that should not be retried.
- Keep direction implementation-ready but do not write the implementation. Do not commit, push, call external services, or create a PR.
- Fail only if evidence needed for a responsible correction design is genuinely unavailable; state the concrete blocker so this design state can retry rather than handing an empty plan to the implementer.

Write:
- Guidance: {{run.dir}}/failure-design/guidance-{{run.round}}.md
- Status: {{run.dir}}/failure-design/status-{{run.attempt}}.json

